<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Tafna</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1837">1837</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-conquest-of-algeria">French conquest of Algeria</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tafna">Tafna</a> was signed on 30 May 1837 near the Tafna river between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emir-abdelkader">Emir Abdelkader</a> and General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thomas-robert-bugeaud">Thomas-Robert Bugeaud</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> recognised Abdelkader's authority over most of western and central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a> while keeping <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oran">Oran</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algiers">Algiers</a> and their hinterlands, which freed French troops to attack Constantine. Disputes over the boundary led Abdelkader to resume the war in 1839.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-tafna.jpg" alt="Treaty of Tafna" width="320" height="386" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Chatsam · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Roubaix_marie_eleonore_godefroid_roubaix_portrait_abdelkader_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
